  ('mathematics/de1-laplace-shifting-theorem', 'mathematics', 'mathematics/differential-equations-1', 2000549, 'formula', 4, false, 'State the **shifting theorem** (the $s$-shift) for the Laplace transform.', 'If $F(s) = \mathcal{L}\{f\}(s)$ exists for $s > c$, then $\mathcal{L}\{e^{at}f(t)\}(s) = F(s - a)$ for $s > a + c$.

